[Music]  the agents of the naval criminal  investigative service or ncis often have  to make snap decisions when in the  middle of dangerous and intense  situations whether for the sake of their  colleagues or their country several  characters on the cbs procedural commit  morally ambiguous actions over the  course of its staggering 19 seasons and  400 plus episodes however when the sunny  goth forensics investigator abby played  by paulie pared breaks bad in a season 5  episode many fans consider her behavior  controversial while agents gibbs dinozzo  and david portrayed by mark harmon  michael weatherly and cody depablo  respectively are characters which openly  struggle with personal demons or family  complications abby is a generous and  playful person but everything seems to  take a sudden turn in the episode dog  tags the episode kicks off with the team  executing a warrant on a house only to  find their suspect mauled to death  inside the suspect's dog butch then  attacks agent mcgee portrayed by sean  murray landing a serious bite on his  neck and wrist mcgee defends himself by  non-fatally shooting the canine but  butch's behavior convinces the rest of  the ncis team that he killed the suspect  all except abby furious with mcgee abby  is convinced that the dog who she  affectionately renames jethro did  nothing wrong and she risks her career  to prove his innocence in 2019 a comment  thread titled what the hell abby  appeared on the subreddit for ncis a  community which hosts over 12 600  members as of 2022 a user took umbrage  with an early scene in the episode  during the scene in question abby  berates mcgee when she learns he shot  the dog and doesn't believe him when he  tries to explain the severity of the  attack while the commenter felt that  abby meant well they also claimed that  the dog almost tore mcgee's arm off and  gave him a lifelong fear of dogs but she  doesn't show the slightest bit of  sympathy to her friend and she never  apologizes numerous other redditors  affirmed that abby's treatment of mcgee  made little sense considering the  character's existing professional and  personal relationships another user  commented on the thread saying that abby  forces more like threatens mcgee to  actually contribute for flowers for the  dog and later forces him to take him in  as a pet another commenter referred to a  scene where abby tells mcgee sometimes  you have to look at the reality in front  of you and just accept it the user  points out the irony of these words  since abby doesn't follow her own advice  despite mcgee telling abby the truth  about what happened they exclaim this  dog she just med is more important than  her friend co-worker and ex-lover  general consensus seems to be that even  though abby eventually proves the dog's  innocence that doesn't mean mcgee should  have to adopt a semi-hostile animal who  attacked him in fact numerous fans  revealed how abby's attitude in this  particular episode started her  transformation into a selfish petulant  person they didn't enjoy watching an  august 2021 post on the ncis subreddit  includes a comment from a user who wrote  cracked and dog tags are the  quintessential abby is a petulant child  just cuz episodes just a few months  earlier an entire thread dedicated to  dog tags popped up on the ncis subreddit  the user wrote at length about how the  entire episode made them dislike abby  they voiced distaste for abby's highly  unprofessional attitude when the time  came to surrender the dog and went on to  detail their distaste for how abby  completely neglects mcgee's feelings the  post elicited a comment from another  user that appears to best sum up the  entire issue with dog tags and the way  it depicts abby i always loved early  season's abby but as the show progressed  i felt like she got more selfish  childish and unprofessional it was a  weird regression like they tried too  hard to make her quirky check out one of  our newest videos right here plus even  more looper videos about ncis are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one  [Music]

